WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.680
Where should you live in a zombie apocalypse?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.360
As with most things, location is&nbsp;
everything, and not all communities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.320
on The Walking Dead are created equal. Here&nbsp;
is a ranking of each one from worst to best.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.980
Huge points get taken off for this community&nbsp;
because they don't allow themselves to settle&nbsp;down.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.560
This faction decided early on that they&nbsp;
didn't want to bother with hanging onto the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:28.080
that was. Instead, they decide to cede control of&nbsp;
the planet to the zombies by living among them.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:33.280
Rather than build walls to keep the walkers out,&nbsp;
they wear cured-flesh masks that allow them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.520
blend in with the dead, even strategically&nbsp;
herding them for their benefit at times.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:43.840
Part of their philosophy is that humanity needs to&nbsp;
get back to its more animalistic roots. Therefore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.480
they operate on a societal basis of hierarchy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.320
with an Alpha leading their every&nbsp;
move and making all their decisions.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.720
Although they successfully eliminate&nbsp;
walkers as a threat to their daily lives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:00.080
it just doesn't feel like a great way to live. The&nbsp;
worst part is that a Whisperer is always at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:05.120
mercy of their Alpha. If Alpha decides the herd&nbsp;
is moving one way, that's the way they're going.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:10.553
If Alpha decides to start a war with well-armed&nbsp;
humans, they're going to war. In short, there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.553 --> 00:01:15.680
not much difference between a Whisperer and a&nbsp;
regular zombie other than, technically, freedom.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.160
"We are the walking dead."

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.120
This is a great example of something that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.960
sounds terrific on paper being&nbsp;
absolutely awful in practice.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.920
At the onset of the apocalypse, a handful of&nbsp;
police officers in Atlanta manage to maintain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:35.840
their rank in society amongst a hospital skeleton&nbsp;
crew as the city falls into anarchy. Their leader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.520
Dawn Lerner, has the respect of her&nbsp;
fellow officers due to her rank,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.960
which means increasingly less&nbsp;
with each passing, lawless day.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:48.320
Eventually, supplies dwindle and Dawn implements&nbsp;
a system of taking survivors in for medical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.400
treatment, only to force them to pay off&nbsp;
the debt they've incurred for being saved.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.800
Unable to keep the tense community afloat,&nbsp;
Dawn resorts to more hostile measures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.920
basically enslaving anyone that the police&nbsp;
find. In a world where humanity is scarce and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:06.240
decisions are being made on a life-or-death&nbsp;
level, having to defer to the judgment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.400
and power of a former law enforcement&nbsp;
officer just sounds like a nightmare.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:15.520
For Dawn and her citizens, life becomes&nbsp;
about serving a singular goal — keeping her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:20.000
in power. That seems like a great deal&nbsp;
for Dawn, less so for everyone else.

00:02:20.766 --> 00:02:25.040
Woodbury gets credit for being one of the&nbsp;
first safe havens built from the ground up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:28.800
after the onset of the apocalypse.&nbsp;
Early on in the show's timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.600
The Governor leads a small group of people to&nbsp;
clear out, fortify and make the town somewhat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.680
self-sustaining at a time when most&nbsp;
other people were wandering the woods.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.320
Under The Governor's leadership, they even&nbsp;
manage to plant crops and get the power back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:47.520
on so that some small slice of normal life&nbsp;
was restored to a little more than 70 people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.600
However, although comfortable, the&nbsp;
residents of Woodbury are completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.080
unaware of the day-to-day danger they&nbsp;
face — mostly from their insane leader.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:00.960
"I'm sorry, it's just this&nbsp;
place… I can't stay here."&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:04.453
"Why?"
"The Governor. He is not what he seems to be."

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.520
The viewers know The Governor to be a heinous&nbsp;
individual capable of horrific crimes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.120
However, the average person who sees&nbsp;
tomatoes growing in their neighborhood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.440
probably isn't looking too closely at where&nbsp;
the latest shipment of supplies came from.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.920
This ignorance comes to a head during the&nbsp;
war with Rick Grimes' group in the prison.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.080
The citizens of Woodbury think themselves&nbsp;
the good guys when they launch their attack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.080
but some of the survivors of the battle&nbsp;
are cut down by The Governor himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:33.145
Not exactly a community where&nbsp;
you can depend on your leader.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:38.000
Once you survive the apocalypse, the&nbsp;
question becomes what kind of day-to-day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.000
life is acceptable for you to survive&nbsp;
in? For the members of The Scavengers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.040
the answer to that question has a pretty low bar.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:49.040
While the people around them are clearing&nbsp;
out prisons, factories and small towns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.560
a woman calling herself Jadis&nbsp;
decides to claim a junkyard.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.760
On paper, it sounds bad. However, if you're&nbsp;
looking to survive, it provides security as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:03.200
well as resources like scrap metal and even&nbsp;
some food. Meanwhile, Jadis' policy of rarely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.520
risking her people's lives or even revealing&nbsp;
their presence to the world means that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:12.400
avoid conflict while living in relative&nbsp;
comfort with plenty of essential supplies.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:17.680
Eventually, though, the war in the area becomes&nbsp;
so large that Jadis and her people fall into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:22.640
hands of The Saviors. Until then, however,&nbsp;
Jadis has a resource-heavy community full of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:28.160
loyal people who stayed out of sight and therefore&nbsp;
out of mind. They were even making groovy artwork&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:33.040
and adopting weird eccentricities like only&nbsp;
speaking in broken English. These are things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:37.548
that people have the luxury to experiment&nbsp;
with once safety isn't really a concern.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.200
Speaking of odd diction choices in the apocalypse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:45.760
The Kingdom takes the cake by forcing its&nbsp;
most loyal members to adopt a Renaissance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:50.160
Fair style of English as they pledge&nbsp;
fealty to their founder and king, Ezekiel.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:56.154
"What do you think of the Kingdom?&nbsp;
What do you think of the king?"

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:01.040
While having to perform a character as&nbsp;
family members die and society crumbles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:06.400
all around you is challenging to say the least,&nbsp;
The Kingdom is one of the nicer places to live.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:11.920
Early in the apocalypse, Ezekiel sees potential&nbsp;
in an abandoned school and fortifies it as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.880
place to build a community. Unfortunately,&nbsp;
it isn't around a lot of natural resources,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:21.600
nor is it in the most defensible spot. However,&nbsp;
that doesn't stop him from putting in the work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:26.000
and turning it into a self-sustaining&nbsp;
safe haven. Unfortunately, his hold on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.560
The Kingdom is interrupted by The Saviors&nbsp;
coming in and demanding a piece of the pie.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:34.240
It doesn't take long before the resources&nbsp;
and good nature of The Kingdom and its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:38.240
citizens dwindle. While the community&nbsp;
gets credit for changing with the times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:43.040
the fact is that Ezekiel invests long term&nbsp;
in a place with a short expiration date.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.480
The Prison may seem like a great place to live,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:51.040
and Rick and his group of survivors do their&nbsp;
best to make it one for a long time. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:54.560
the logistics of maintaining a&nbsp;
prison are a constant struggle.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:59.840
For one, the place was designed to be maintained&nbsp;
by a large staff of guards, cooks, administrators,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:05.040
and more. When in doubt, prison labor filled in&nbsp;
the gaps. When the survivors arrive, it's up to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:09.920
a little more than a dozen people to manage a&nbsp;
massive facility. While blocking off a section&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:14.560
of the prison is easy enough, they are constantly&nbsp;
plagued by walkers getting past the gates.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:18.400
Meanwhile, its curbside appeal makes&nbsp;
it a constant target for attacks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:23.600
which is ultimately how the prison falls. In a&nbsp;
desperate world, having something as shiny and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:28.720
secure as a prison is too often an invitation&nbsp;
for outsiders to take what isn't theirs.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:34.000
A place can be as safe as possible from walkers,&nbsp;
but as the show constantly reminds its audience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.160
human beings are the real threat in this world.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.480
The community of Oceanside is&nbsp;
created after another settlement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:43.440
falls to the ruthless tactics of the Savior Simon.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:47.920
After suffering a defeat that sees every&nbsp;
male member of their society executed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:51.520
the women and children flee to&nbsp;
re-establish themselves elsewhere.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:55.680
They become the first group on this&nbsp;
list to utilize their natural geography&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:00.240
by putting the ocean at their back to prevent&nbsp;
walkers coming at them from every side.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:04.000
They decide that sharing what they&nbsp;
have with the world is no longer an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:08.640
option because someone like Simon will&nbsp;
eventually strong arm their way into taking it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:12.800
As a result, they spend most of their&nbsp;
time doing the bare minimum to survive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:16.960
while getting rid of anyone that might make&nbsp;
their presence known to the rest of the world.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:21.680
Unfortunately, their main concern is staying&nbsp;
hidden, which prevents them from really building&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:27.600
the Oceanside community into something grand&nbsp;
until after Rick's war with Negan. Even then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:30.480
resources are scarce and Oceanside becomes little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:34.400
more than a stopping point for people&nbsp;
to travel to more secure locations.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:37.440
However, the community gets a&nbsp;
lot of credit for being naturally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:41.280
fortified from the water as well as&nbsp;
standing tall in the face of defeat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:45.364
Oceanside also gets top marks for&nbsp;
its resilience and tactical position.

00:07:46.185 --> 00:07:49.680
Fortified walls, an endless&nbsp;
supply of fighters, resources,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:53.440
and a somewhat merit-based economy.&nbsp;
If that sounds like a good time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:58.160
The Sanctuary might be up your alley. Of&nbsp;
course, it's not all sunshine and lollipops.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:01.360
Members of The Sanctuary are&nbsp;
asked to join an incredibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:06.080
unforgiving cult that promises safety&nbsp;
in exchange for entering a debt system&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:10.720
similar to that of Grady Memorial Hospital. If&nbsp;
you decide that you're not happy with the deal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:15.920
you can always run. However, Negan and The Saviors&nbsp;
are powerful enough to collect on their debts.

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:21.040
Unfortunately, all it takes is a run-in with Rick&nbsp;
Grimes for everything to crumble. The problem with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:26.000
ruling by fear is that, once you encounter someone&nbsp;
that isn't afraid to take a few hits, you can't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:31.920
just take your ball and go home. Negan understands&nbsp;
that, which is why he wages total war on Rick and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:37.120
his alliance of communities. He knows that there&nbsp;
is no way to continue ruling by force if there is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:42.240
an equally powerful civilization in the area with&nbsp;
a more enlightened view on corporal punishment.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.080
Similar to The Sanctuary, Terminus is a large,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:51.280
brick facility that is easily fortified and&nbsp;
manned by people to ensure the dead stayed out.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:55.760
Its people don't even need to risk venturing&nbsp;
out into the world for supplies. Everything they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.760 --> 00:09:00.640
need in terms of weapons, equipment and, yes,&nbsp;
food, is delivered right to their front door.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:06.000
After resorting to cannibalism following a&nbsp;
horrific attack, leader Gareth advertises Terminus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:10.880
as a safe haven for survivors. That's just the&nbsp;
sales pitch, however. Anyone who makes it to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:16.320
Terminus has to give up their gear before getting&nbsp;
made into a feast for real Terminus residents.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:21.920
Gareth builds a society that is sustainable and&nbsp;
secure. However, the cost of entry is becoming a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:27.360
straight up cannibal. One can only survive so&nbsp;
long on morally questionable societal means,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:31.124
but Gareth manages to make it&nbsp;
last for a surprisingly long time.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:35.680
This safe haven has literally&nbsp;
everything. Alexandria is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:39.120
community that was converted from&nbsp;
an upscale suburban neighborhood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:44.480
originally designed for sustainability. Once&nbsp;
the apocalypse hits, a professor of architecture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:49.840
redesigns and fortifies the walls to ensure&nbsp;
that both people and walkers can't get in.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:53.600
There's enough space and empty houses&nbsp;
for people to really set down some roots,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:56.880
knowing that they don't have to&nbsp;
worry about the wasteland outside.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:01.760
Plus, its location near a mall means years&nbsp;
of guaranteed supplies before needing to look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:07.360
elsewhere. In short, Alexandria ticks off all&nbsp;
the boxes of both safety and comfort. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:11.840
being comfortable and safe isn't always&nbsp;
the best thing for people in an apocalypse.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:16.240
Similar to the prison, when you have something&nbsp;
that looks this great to a desperate outsider,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:21.360
it will forever be a target. Since settling&nbsp;
down in Alexandria, its citizens have done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:25.840
nothing but fight the outside world&nbsp;
to varying degrees of success. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:31.167
if you like a lot of danger and excitement in&nbsp;
your life, Alexandria might be the place for you.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:35.600
It may not be the flashiest, it&nbsp;
may not be the most comfortable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:40.960
but it's definitely survived and thrived more&nbsp;
than any other community with more potential.

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:44.960
The Hilltop starts out as a historic&nbsp;
museum house in Virginia before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:48.960
the apocalypse turns it into a safe&nbsp;
zone. When the military abandons it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:52.560
the survivors decide it's the&nbsp;
perfect place to build a stronghold.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:57.120
Its location in the wilderness means that&nbsp;
large invasions by walkers aren't likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:01.600
and easy to see coming if the impossible&nbsp;
does occur. Survivors can't really sneak up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:06.240
on the place and if they did, they'd have large&nbsp;
walls and guards with weapons to contend with.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:10.880
The community is even self-sustaining, with&nbsp;
fertile ground and dependable crops without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:15.760
the need to venture outside. However, the true&nbsp;
strength of The Hilltop is in its leadership.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:20.560
For all his flaws, Gregory was the exact&nbsp;
person Hilltop needed to establish and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:24.720
secure the safe haven. However, when he&nbsp;
proves ineffective as a wartime leader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:27.760
the people are lucky enough&nbsp;
to see Maggie take charge.

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:32.400
When all else is failing around them,&nbsp;
The Hilltop digs in and manage to survive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:35.840
while other, more seemingly&nbsp;
secure and stocked communities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:40.480
fall like dominoes. Not only is it a&nbsp;
well-built place to live, but it's led&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:45.600
by people who are just hardened enough to keep&nbsp;
it safe without resorting to drastic measures.

